     "description": "Steve Yzerman, the Detroit Red Wings' captain for an unparalleled 22 seasons, was an unstoppable force on the ice. He reached the 50-goal mark in five different seasons, amassing an incredible 692 career goals. During the 1992-93 season, Yzerman notched his 50th goal in a game against Edmonton with a play that showcased his skill and elusiveness. Receiving a pass in full stride, Yzerman streaked down the ice, deftly maneuvered around a defenseman, and fired a shot five-hole to cap off the milestone in style.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
